;; Overlay lock for the amu --jvm-free emitter checkout (NOT the app closure).
;;
;; Why this file exists: bin/amu at the compiler-pin.edn :amu pin (8435eafb)
;; derives its resolution root from its own location (bin/amu line 407:
;; `root = path.resolve(dirname(realpath(__filename)), "..")`), so
;; `resolveWithLock` reads <amu-checkout>/deps-lock.edn -- amu's own stale
;; lock, never the app's deps-lock.edn. amu's lock names deleted split repos
;; (abi.git, kotoba-kir.git, ... all 404), which fails the emit with
;; "git clone failed ... could not read Username". Regenerating the app's
;; lock cannot fix that path; only this overlay, copied over
;; <amu-checkout>/deps-lock.edn before compile (see scripts/ci-jvm-free-emit),
;; reaches the resolver that actually runs.
;;
;; Provenance (no JVM needed to audit): entry set = amu@8435eafb's own
;; deps-lock.edn coordinates (21, same order); :lock/deps-digest =
;; sha256(amu@8435eafb deps.edn bytes), verified byte-identical via fetch.
;; Nine entries are verbatim from the app's deps-lock.edn (resolvable,
;; zero dead URLs); the other twelve map the deleted compiler splits to
;; their monorepo successors at the same kotoba.git commit the app uses
;; (4b2d03ed), with kir absorbed into lib/kotoba.osaho (the only home of
;; src/kotoba/kir/* at that commit). Every recorded path was verified to
;; exist at its recorded commit with `git ls-tree`.
;;
;; Bound to amu@8435eafb's deps.edn bytes: bumping :amu in compiler-pin.edn
;; requires re-deriving this file against the new pin's deps.edn digest.
